eam came from another family. The tests check settles the behaviour criteria, and the seats read the code against all five criteria.\nran: tests: reported in 2s; correctness: reported in 32s; redteam: reported in 12s\nplan check: PASS \u2014 no deviations\n\nFindings:\n- tests (check): I ran 13 touched test files with PYTHONPATH=src and without building the project, so nothing was written to build/. 202 passed, 8 network tests were deselected, and 2 failed for an environment reason only. Both failing tests spawn `python -I`, which ignores PYTHONPATH. I re-ran their scripts with src on sys.path and both pass. Positive control: adding `import doifetch.sources.openalex` to a copy of naming.py makes the no-import check fail.\n  - Naming fallback (criterion 1): naming.py imports `_openalex`, never the source module (naming.py:10,130-133).\n  - Fall-through (criterion 2): openalex.py `_fetch` loops over the distinct `pdf_url` values. A transport error, a non-200 status or a failed PDF check moves it to the next location.\n  - Key (criterion 3): the only way the key reaches a message is `_http.HttpError`, whose text includes the urlencoded URL. `get_work` replaces the raw, quote and quote_plus forms with *** and raises `from None`. The refusal messages name the variable and the file path, never the key. The PDF-location URLs carry no key.\n  - Conformance (criterion 4): `openalex` is in the conformance SOURCES.\n  - One list (criterion 5): `--source` choices are `[*SOURCES, \"all\"]`, and SOURCES/ACCEPTS are built from one `_MODULES` tuple.\n- correctness: clear, all five criteria met. `consider:` the key file reader `_key_from_file` (src/doifetch/sources/_openalex.py:38) catches only OSError. A key file that is not valid UTF-8 would raise UnicodeDecodeError up through `get_metadata` into `resolve_name`. That breaks naming's best-effort contract. The source path is safe because of its catch-all. The fix is to catch `(OSError, ValueError)`. No real user scenario was shown, so this stays below the bar.\n- redteam: clear. No path prints or logs the credential, and both the raw and URL-encoded forms are scrubbed (code-read only, tests=not-run).\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 1m54s\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=2 tokens=na cost~=$na\nseat: correctness \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=sonnet \u00b7 model=anthropic/sonnet \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: redteam \u00b7 runtime=codex \u00b7 family=openai \u00b7 route=gpt-6-luna \u00b7 model=openai/gpt-6-luna \u00b7 status: ran\n"}

